250820:

Design principles:

- Keeping as much code out of the code-generated sections
- Being able to debug generated code easilly
- Keeping the dev cycle tight and fast (build -> run -> debug)


250816:

It is possible to call the "mcdisplay functions", and they do seem to work
correctly. The result is printing to the console, and we want to capture that
data into an array of line segment pairs. (Arguably, multiple arrays
depending on type, but for now.)

The current "component" API and corresponding library functions:
                                                NOTE:
    #define magnify     mcdis_magnify           does nothing
    #define line        mcdis_line              very useful, produces the segment (anchor) pair
    #define dashed_line mcdis_dashed_line       falls back to mcdis_line
    #define multiline   mcdis_multiline         pruduces a sequence of anchors (...)
    #define rectangle   mcdis_rectangle         falls back to mcdis_multiline
    #define box         mcdis_box               falls back to mcdis_rectangle and mcdis_multiline
    #define circle      mcdis_circle            outputs an abstract code to the terminal
    #define Circle      mcdis_Circle            falls back to mcdis_line
    #define cylinder    mcdis_cylinder          falls back to mcdis_Circle, mcdis_line
    #define cone        mcdis_cone              falls back to mcdis_Circle, mcdis_line
    #define sphere      mcdis_sphere            falls back to mcdis_Circle, mcdis_line

Typical signatures would be: 

    void mcdis_line(double x1, double y1, double z1, double x2, double y2, double z2);
    void mcdis_circle(char *plane, double x, double y, double z, double r);
    void mcdis_multiline(int count, ...);
    void mcdis_Circle(double x, double y, double z, double r, double nx, double ny, double nz);

Thus we need to replace the intrinsic ones to produce line-segment anchor pairs, specifically:

    mcdis_line
    mcdis_multiline

In addition, the use of mcdis_circle, and perhaps a few others (not used 
in PSI_DMC, apparantly), should be transitioned to mcdis_Circle (capital C).
The latter generates lines, while the former prints a "circle" call,
effectively delegating implementation to the external tool. But this API
is bad and also redundant.
We can re-implement these calls to forward to the more complete mcdis_ calls.


